    "title": "Aromatic Moroccan Sweet Fruit Stew with Honey and Almonds",
    "readyInMinutes": 65,
    "servings": 6,
    "summary": "This fragrant <b>Moroccan sweet fruit stew</b> offers an enchanting conclusion to an elaborate dinner, blending honey-poached stone fruits with aromatic spices. Known traditionally as a dessert tagine, this rich preparation simmers tender <b>dried figs</b>, plump apricots, prunes, and sweet dates in a delicate syrup infused with <b>orange blossom water</b>, cinnamon sticks, cardamom, and saffron. As the fruits absorb the golden nectar, they soften into a luxurious, warm dessert course served alongside crunchy <b>toasted blanched almonds</b> and bright pistachios. Fresh mint sprigs and vibrant pomegranate seeds provide a refreshing contrast to the deeply aromatic, caramelised syrup. Perfect for celebrations, this recipe can be prepared in advance and gently rewarmed just before serving to release its full aromatic perfume. Enjoy this classic North African confection with a pot of traditional mint tea for a truly memorable culinary grand finale that balances fruity sweetness with warm spice.",
